.\" Revision: 3
.TH JPI2EXCEL.SH 1 "September 29, 2026" "JPI2Excel 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jpi2excel.sh \- validate JP Instruments downloads and export CSV or Excel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jpi2excel.sh
.RB [ \-\-info ]
.I action
.RI [ options ]
.IR file.JPI " ..."
.br
.B jpi2excel.sh \-\-info
.RI [ options ]
.IR file.JPI " ..."
.br
.B jpi2excel.sh \-\-help
.br
.B jpi2excel.sh \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jpi2excel.sh
is a Bash wrapper for the JPI2Excel Python command-line program.
It locates
.B jpi2excel.py
in its own directory and runs it with
.B python3
from PATH, forwarding arguments and preserving the Python program's exit status.
It does not change the caller's working directory.
Relative input and output paths are relative to that directory.
.PP
At least one action is required.
.B \-\-info
may run alone or alongside one other action.
All other actions are mutually exclusive; adding
.B \-\-info
does not permit two other actions.
Input files are processed as a collection of flights.
A corrupt file is rejected in its entirety before any of its flights are
exported; processing continues for other inputs.
Duplicate flight numbers across files are retained, with a nonfatal warning
and distinct output names.
.PP
Current decoding supports legacy single-engine EDM-700/800 layouts with
fuel-unit code 0 (U.S. gallons), an eight-field alarm record, and no protocol
record.
Other models, multi-engine layouts, and unvalidated formats fail explicitly.
The recorded model code is preserved, including code 700 in EDM-800 downloads.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-info
Print labeled file and flight properties, one per line, in the form
.IR "Label: value" .
Include identifiers, download time, units, alarms, raw header fields,
flight counts, and per-flight configuration such as recording interval,
rated horsepower, monitored-cylinder count, IAT/CDT presence, and TIT count.
Also report logical and physical binary boundaries and final-block slack.
TIT channel count is not assumed to equal physical turbocharger count.
.B \-\-flights
limits the per-flight details; file properties, raw headers, alarms, and counts
still describe the entire input file.
Short flights may be inspected regardless of the export duration cutoff.
.PP
Info is printed before listing, validation results, or export work.
The accompanying action retains its own behavior: listing includes every
flight, validation checks complete files, and workbook Summary remains complete.
When paired with
.B \-\-help
or
.BR \-\-version ,
help/version is printed first, followed by info if input files were supplied.
Without input files, only help/version is printed.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List every flight's source, number, start date and time, duration, and
.B GPS
or
.BR "No GPS" .
Sort by flight number, placing flights shorter than five minutes last.
The five-minute listing split does not change with
.BR \-\-minimum-duration .
.TP
.B \-\-validate
Validate ASCII checksums, binary flight headers and records, directory
allocations, physical block framing, and the end marker.
Valid unused bytes in the final physical block are accepted and excluded
from flight decoding; see
.BR jpi (5).
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Write one CSV file per selected flight.
.TP
.B \-\-xls
Write one XLSX workbook containing all selected flights from all valid
inputs, one worksheet per flight, and a Summary sheet.
Summary contains the file and flight properties available through
.BR \-\-info ,
including properties of flights excluded from the export selection.
The output is modern XLSX, despite the option's spelling.
.TP
.B \-\-xls-separate
Write one XLSX workbook per selected flight, containing only its flight
worksheet and no Summary sheet.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and options; no input is required.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version; no input is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-flights " selection"
Select
.B all
(the default), comma-separated flight numbers, inclusive colon-separated
ranges, or a combination such as
.BR 393,395:398 .
Numbers must be in the range 0 through 65535.
Selection applies across the input collection; all occurrences of a matching
number are selected.
A requested flight not found in valid inputs is an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " engine"
Default:
.BR all .
For the supported single-engine installation,
.BR left ,
.BR center ,
.BR right ,
or any one positive engine number selects that engine.
Requesting multiple engines is an error in this release.
.TP
.BI \-\-minimum-duration " minutes"
Set the minimum export duration and the qualifying-flight count for
.BR \-\-info .
The argument is a finite nonnegative number of minutes, including fractions;
the default is 5.
A flight exactly at the threshold qualifies.
An all-flights selection skips shorter flights.
Explicitly selecting a shorter flight is an error;
use 0 to include all durations.
Listing still includes every flight.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " path"
Specify the output path when exactly one output file will be created.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-output-dir .
Existing destinations are never overwritten.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " directory"
Specify an existing output directory.
The default is the current directory.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Write additional flight configuration, duration, and export/skip counts to
standard error.
.PP
Flight and engine selection apply to
.B \-\-info
and export actions.
Output-path options require an export action.
Use
.B \-\-
to separate options from input filenames beginning with a hyphen.
.SH OUTPUT
Default combined workbook name:
.BR JPI2Excel.xlsx .
Separate files use
.I source-stem_Flight_number.csv
or
.IR source-stem_Flight_number.xlsx .
Numeric suffixes distinguish collisions within a batch.
Existing destinations cause an error.
An all-flights selection with no qualifying flights creates no output and
succeeds unless another input failed.
.PP
CSV and flight worksheets have this column order, omitting absent sensors:
.PP
.nf
Sample, DeltaT, DateTime, MAP, RPM, EGTs, TITs, CHTs,
FF, %HP, OAT, CDT, IAT, Oil P, Oil T, Batt, Used,
MARK, Diff, Cold, Limits, Lat, Lon, Alt, Speed
.fi
.PP
Sample numbering begins at 1.
.B DeltaT is numeric elapsed seconds since flight start.
It is never elapsed minutes or an Excel fraction of a day.
Timestamps preserve source-clock values without an invented timezone.
Excel stores actual datetime cells displayed through seconds, without
milliseconds; CSV stores ISO-style text.
.PP
Cylinder labels are
.BR "EGT 1" ,
.BR "CHT 1" ,
and so on.
A single TIT channel is labeled
.BR TIT ;
multiple channels are labeled
.BR "TIT 1" ,
.BR "TIT 2" ,
and so on.
Available navigation columns are last.
Header-declared channels without decoded values retain blank columns and
produce warnings.
Unchanged initialized sensor readings retain their reconstructed values.
.PP
.B Limits
contains semicolon-separated violations of thresholds present in the file,
for example
.BR "CHT 3;TIT 2;BAT-L" .
Parameters with both high and low thresholds use
.B \-H
or
.B \-L
suffixes.
Equality to a threshold is not a violation.
Missing thresholds are not invented.
.PP
Excel sheets freeze row 1 and columns A and B (cell C2).
Autofilters and cell comments are disabled.
Source units and configuration appear in info/Summary output.
.PP
Flight-column widths follow their data: Sample 60 pixels, DeltaT 55,
DateTime 115, sensor/navigation values 55, and Limits 120.
These widths follow the columns when channels are omitted or added.
Excel character-width settings are calibrated to the supplied macOS
Calibri 11 reference workbook; rendering can vary with font and viewer.
.PP
Summary columns Source, Input, Property, and Value use widths of 85, 50,
225, and 450 pixels respectively.
The Value column wraps text.
Input is the one-based number of each successfully read source in input order.
It distinguishes repeated inputs or files sharing the same basename;
it is not a flight number.
A flight may contain at most 1,048,575 data rows in an Excel worksheet;
use CSV if that limit is exceeded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; warnings are nonfatal.
Most failures use the platform's numeric
.B errno
value, which may differ between operating systems.
.TP
.B ENOENT
Source or destination directory not found.
.TP
.B EPERM
Permission denied reading input or writing output.
.TP
.B EEXIST
Destination already exists.
.TP
.B ENOTDIR
Destination directory or parent is not a directory.
.TP
.B EISDIR
A file path names a directory.
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid, incompatible, or missing arguments.
.TP
.B ECANCELED
Interrupted by SIGINT or SIGTERM.
Any partial output file is retained.
.TP
.B EDOM
Requested flight or engine is unavailable.
.TP
.B EILSEQ
Invalid input structure or checksum.
This status takes precedence over other batch failures, even if valid inputs
were exported successfully.
.TP
.B EOPNOTSUPP
No action was specified, or the input format is unsupported.
.TP
.B EFBIG
A flight exceeds the Excel row limit.
.TP
.B 200
Uncategorized application or missing-dependency error.
.TP
.B 201
An explicitly selected flight is shorter than the minimum duration.
.SH EXAMPLES
From the repository root:
.PP
.nf
\&./pgms/jpi2excel.sh \-\-list testdata/U260919.JPI
\&./pgms/jpi2excel.sh \-\-validate testdata/*.JPI
\&./pgms/jpi2excel.sh \-\-info \-\-flights 418 testdata/U260919.JPI
.fi
.PP
Export selected flights, including the short flight 417:
.PP
.nf
\&./pgms/jpi2excel.sh \-\-info \-\-csv \-\-flights 415:418 \e
    \-\-minimum-duration 0 \-\-output-dir /existing/output \e
    testdata/U260919.JPI
.fi
.PP
Create a combined workbook using the default five-minute cutoff:
.PP
.nf
\&./pgms/jpi2excel.sh \-\-xls \-\-output flights.xlsx \e
    testdata/U260731.JPI testdata/U260828.JPI
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B pgms/jpi2excel.sh
Bash launcher; requires Bash and Python 3.10 or later.
.TP
.B pgms/jpi2excel.py
Python entry point next to the wrapper.
.TP
.B src/jpi2excel/
Application source.
.TP
.B ../JPI-Parser/
Optional read-only sibling dependency used by the development launcher
when JPI-Parser is not installed.
It must match the clean pinned revision.
.PP
The selected Python environment requires JPI-Parser and
.BR openpyxl .
The wrapper does not activate a virtual environment; activate one before
invoking it if needed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR jpi (5)
.PP
